msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Finds the factor settings that maximize the composite desirability of the "
"included responses, based on the fitted model of each response. Continuous "
"factors are searched within their observed range; all combinations of "
"discrete factor levels are tried."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"The responses to optimize. For each response, the individual desirability "
"(between 0 and 1) is set by the goal, bounds, target and weight. The "
"composite desirability is the weighted geometric mean of the individual "
"desirabilities, with the importances (normalized to sum to 1) as weights."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Whether to maximize or minimize the response, or to hit a target value."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Response value below which the individual desirability is 0. Used for the "
"goals maximize and target. Only editable with 'Set all bounds manually'; "
"otherwise the minimum of the observed response is used."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Response value at which the individual desirability is 1. Always editable "
"for the goal target. For maximize and minimize only editable with 'Set all "
"targets manually'; otherwise the maximum or minimum of the observed response "
"is used."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Response value above which the individual desirability is 0. Used for the "
"goals minimize and target. Only editable with 'Set all bounds manually'; "
"otherwise the maximum of the observed response is used."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Shape of the individual desirability between bound and target (0.1 to 10). "
"With 1 it increases linearly; larger values require the response to be "
"closer to the target for a high desirability, smaller values are more "
"lenient."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Relative importance of the response in the composite desirability (0.1 to "
"10). Only enabled with more than one response."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Show the optimizer settings per response and the optimal solution: the "
"factor levels with the highest composite desirability, that desirability, "
"and the predicted (fitted) responses at these levels."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid "Confidence and prediction intervals"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Predicted response at the optimal (or manually set) factor levels, with the "
"confidence interval for the mean response and the prediction interval for a "
"single new run. Blocks are averaged out; covariates are held at their mean."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Show a matrix of plots with one column per factor. The top row shows the "
"composite desirability, the other rows one per response. Each plot varies "
"one factor while the other factors are held at the optimal (or manually set) "
"levels, which are marked in red."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "doeAnalysis|"
msgid ""
